{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-mat-17-1","title":"Matthew 17:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":17,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":17,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 The transfiguration of Christ. 14 He heals the lunatic, 22 foretells his own passion, 24 and pays tribute.</p>\n<p>after.Luke, taking in both the day of the preceding discourse and that of the transfiguration, as well as the six intermediate ones, says it was eight days after.</p>\n<p>Mr 9:2-13; Lu 9:28-36 Peter. 26:37; Mr 5:37; Lu 8:51; 2Co 13:1 an high. 2Pe 1:18</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-17-2","title":"Matthew 17:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":17,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":17,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>transfigured. Lu 9:29; Ro 12:2; Php 2:6,7; *Gr: his face. 28:3; Ex 34:29-35; Joh 1:14; 17:24; Ac 26:13-15; Re 1:13-17; 10:1 Re 19:12,13; 20:11 raiment. Ps 104:2; Mr 9:3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-17-3","title":"Matthew 17:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":17,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":17,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>behold. Mr 9:4; Lu 9:30,31 Moses. 11:13,14; De 18:18; 34:5,6,10; Lu 24:27,44; Joh 1:17; 5:45-47 2Co 3:7-11; Heb 3:1-6 Elias. 10-13; 1Ki 17:1; 18:36-40; 2Ki 2:11-14; Mal 4:5 Elijah. Lu 1:17; 9:33; 16:16</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-17-4","title":"Matthew 17:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":17,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":17,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>answered. Mr 9:5,6; Lu 9:33 it is. Ex 33:18,19; Ps 4:6; 16:11; 63:1-5; Isa 33:17; Zec 9:17; Joh 14:8,9 Joh 17:24; Php 1:23; 1Jo 3:2; Re 21:23; 22:3-5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-17-5","title":"Matthew 17:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":17,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":17,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>behold. Ex 40:34,35; 1Ki 8:10-12; Ps 18:10,11; Lu 9:34; Ac 1:9; Re 1:7 a voice. Ex 19:19; De 4:11,12; 5:22; Job 38:1; Ps 81:7; Joh 5:37; 12:28-30 Ac 9:3-6 This. 3:17; Mr 1:11; 9:7; Lu 3:22; 9:35; Joh 3:16,35; 5:20-23; Eph 1:6 Col 1:13; *marg: 2Pe 1:16,17 in whom. 12:18; Isa 42:1,21; Joh 15:9,10 hear. De 18:15,19; Ac 3:22,23; 7:37; Heb 1:1,2; 2:1-3; 5:9; 12:25,26</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-17-6","title":"Matthew 17:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":17,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":17,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>Le 9:24; Jud 13:20,22; 1Ch 21:16; Eze 3:23; 43:3; Da 8:17; 10:7-9 Da 10:16,17; Ac 22:7; 26:14; 2Pe 1:18</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-17-7","title":"Matthew 17:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":17,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":17,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>touched. Da 8:18; 9:21; 10:10,18; Re 1:17 Arise. Lu 24:5; Ac 9:6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-17-8","title":"Matthew 17:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":17,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":17,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>they saw. Mr 9:8; Lu 9:36; Ac 12:10,11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-17-9","title":"Matthew 17:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":17,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":17,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>Jesus. 16:20; Mr 8:30; 9:9,10; Lu 8:56; 9:21,22 until. 23; 16:21; Lu 18:33,34; 24:46,47</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-17-10","title":"Matthew 17:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":17,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":17,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>Why. 3,4; 11:14; 27:47-49; Mal 4:5,6; Mr 9:11; Joh 1:21,25</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-17-11","title":"Matthew 17:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":17,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":17,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>and restore. Mal 4:6; Lu 1:16,17; 3:3-14; Ac 3:21</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-17-12","title":"Matthew 17:12","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":17,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":17,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>and they. 11:9-15; 21:23-25,32; Mr 9:12,13; 11:30-32; Lu 7:33; Joh 1:11 Joh 5:32-36; Ac 13:24-28 but. 11:2; 14:3-10; Mr 6:14-28; Lu 3:19,20; Ac 7:52 Likewise. 16:21; Isa 53:3-12; Lu 9:21-25; Ac 2:23; 3:14,15; 4:10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-17-13","title":"Matthew 17:13","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":17,"verseStart":13,"chapterEnd":17,"verseEnd":13},"content":"<p>the disciples. 11:14</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-17-14","title":"Matthew 17:14","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":17,"verseStart":14,"chapterEnd":17,"verseEnd":14},"content":"<p>when. Mr 9:14-29; Lu 9:37-43 kneeling. Mr 1:40; 10:17; Ac 10:25,26</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-17-15","title":"Matthew 17:15","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":17,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":17,"verseEnd":15},"content":"<p>have. 15:22; Mr 5:22,23; 9:22; Lu 9:38-42; Joh 4:46,47 for. 4:24; Mr 9:17,18,20-22 he is.[Seleniazomai ,] from [selene ,] the moon, one who was affected with his disorder at the change and full of the moon. This is the case in some kinds of madness and epilepsy. This youth was no doubt epileptic; but it was evidently either produced or taken advantage of by a demon or evil spirit.</p>\n<p>for ofttimes. 8:31,32; Job 1:10-19; 2:7; Mr 5:4,5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-17-16","title":"Matthew 17:16","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":17,"verseStart":16,"chapterEnd":17,"verseEnd":16},"content":"<p>and they. 19,20; 2Ki 4:29-31; Lu 9:40; Ac 3:16; 19:15,16</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-17-17","title":"Matthew 17:17","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":17,"verseStart":17,"chapterEnd":17,"verseEnd":17},"content":"<p>O faithless. 6:30; 8:26; 13:58; 16:8; Mr 9:19; 16:14; Lu 9:41; 24:25; Joh 20:27 Heb 3:16-19 how long shall I be. Ex 10:3; 16:28; Nu 14:11,27; Ps 95:10; Pr 1:22; 6:9; Jer 4:14 Ac 13:18</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-17-18","title":"Matthew 17:18","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":17,"verseStart":18,"chapterEnd":17,"verseEnd":18},"content":"<p>rebuked. 12:22; Mr 1:34; 5:8; 9:25-27; Lu 4:35,36,41; 8:29; 9:42 Ac 16:18; 19:13-15 from. 9:22; 15:28; Joh 4:52,53</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-17-19","title":"Matthew 17:19","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":17,"verseStart":19,"chapterEnd":17,"verseEnd":19},"content":"<p>Mr 4:10; 9:28</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-17-20","title":"Matthew 17:20","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":17,"verseStart":20,"chapterEnd":17,"verseEnd":20},"content":"<p>Because. 17; 14:30,31; Heb 3:19 If. 21:21; Mr 11:23; Lu 17:6; 1Co 12:9; 13:2 faith.That is, as Bp. Pearce well remarks, a thriving and increasing faith, like a grain of mustard seed, which, from being the least of seeds, becomes the greatest of all herbs.</p>\n<p>a grain. 13:31; Mr 4:31 nothing. Mr 9:23; Lu 1:37; 18:27</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-17-21","title":"Matthew 17:21","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":17,"verseStart":21,"chapterEnd":17,"verseEnd":21},"content":"<p>this. 12:45 but. 1Ki 17:20,21; Da 9:3; Mr 9:29; Ac 13:2,3; 14:23; 1Co 7:5; 2Co 11:27 Eph 6:18</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-17-22","title":"Matthew 17:22","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":17,"verseStart":22,"chapterEnd":17,"verseEnd":22},"content":"<p>The Son. 16:21; 20:17,18; Mr 8:31; 9:30,31; 10:33,34; Lu 9:22,44; 18:31-34 Lu 24:6,7,26,46 betrayed. 24:10; 26:16,46; Ac 7:52; 1Co 11:23</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-17-23","title":"Matthew 17:23","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":17,"verseStart":23,"chapterEnd":17,"verseEnd":23},"content":"<p>they shall. Ps 22:15,22-31; Isa 53:7,10-12; Da 9:26; Zec 13:7 the third. Ps 16:10; Joh 2:19; Ac 2:23-31; 1Co 15:3,4 And they were. Joh 16:6,20-22</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-17-24","title":"Matthew 17:24","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":17,"verseStart":24,"chapterEnd":17,"verseEnd":24},"content":"<p>when. Mr 9:33 tribute.\"Gr. didrachma, in value fifteen pence.\"</p>\n<p>Ex 30:13; 38:26 This tribute seems to have been the half shekel which every male among the Jews paid yearly for the support of the temple, and which was continued by them, wherever dispersed, till after the time of Vespasian.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-17-25","title":"Matthew 17:25","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":17,"verseStart":25,"chapterEnd":17,"verseEnd":25},"content":"<p>Yes. 3:15; 22:21; Ro 13:6,7 of their. 1Sa 17:25</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-17-27","title":"Matthew 17:27","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":17,"verseStart":27,"chapterEnd":17,"verseEnd":27},"content":"<p>lest. 15:12-14; Ro 14:21; 15:1-3; 1Co 8:9,13; 9:19-22; 10:32,33; 2Co 6:3 1Th 5:22; Tit 2:7,8 and take. Ge 1:28; 1Ki 17:4; Ps 8:8; Jon 1:17; 2:10; Heb 2:7,8 a piece of money.\"Or, a stater, half an ounce of silver, value 2s. 6d., after 5s. the ounce.\"</p>\n<p>that take. 2Co 8:9; Jas 2:5</p>"}]}